  "notes": "Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim from the official 2024-2025 American International College 'Program Plan' for Sports and Recreation Management (School of Business, Arts and Sciences). Semester totals printed on the plan: 15+15+15+15+16+14+15+15 = 120 credits (TOTAL CREDITS: 120). The program is a Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA; the plan lists the Common Professional Component requirements). The three 'SRMXXXX, any SRM course listed' slots (Junior Spring, Senior Fall, Senior Spring) are three courses chosen from: SRM2801 Sporting Goods Industry, SRM2850 Public Relation and Sport Media, SRM3203 Sports Psychology, SRM3211 Legal Issues in Sports and Recreation Management. Major requirements: MGT3213 Human Resource Management, SRM1600 Introduction to Sport Industry, SRM2600 Event and Facility Management, SRM3210 Sports Marketing, SRM3212 International Aspects of Sports Management, SRM3401 Sports Finance and Economics, SRM4090 Current Issues in Sports Management, plus three SRM electives. The capstone is BUS4899 Business Internship OR MGT4800 Senior Policy Seminar (one in Senior Fall, the other in Senior Spring — both are Common Professional Component requirements, transcribed as printed). MIS1300 Business Analytics with Excel or an elective (Sophomore year flexible). General Education categories per the 2024-2025 plan: Cat 1 Scientific World (math + science with lab), Cat 2 Self and Others, Cat 3 Interdisciplinarity (ENG1202 + INT courses), Cat 4 Arts and Humanities, Cat 5 Professional Readiness (AIC1005/AIC1100 + AIC3005). tccns mirrors the local course code (AIC is in Massachusetts; no TCCNS). transfer_confidence is 'core_only'.",
